# DTF tier manifest: cargo-scan-on-proxy  (artifact-keeper 1.11.0: #4101,
# issue #4097)
# Profile-set: filesystem + the mock-scan-formats upstream (a Cargo sparse
# registry with crates whose Cargo.toml names known coordinates). LOCAL-ONLY:
# the verdicts come from the backend image's bundled Grype and its pre-seeded
# vulnerability DB (no scanner sidecar, no OSV, no internet).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS: before 1.11.0 a Cargo Remote (or a Virtual over one) with
# scan_on_proxy=true streamed every .crate unscanned (200, no X-AK-Scan). 1.11.0
# routes the crate download through the shared inline scan gate: vulnerable ->
# 403 scan_blocked, clean -> 200 X-AK-Scan: clean (immutable cache), a crate
# whose Cargo.toml does not back the requested coordinate -> 423 under
# fail_closed, a crate that disagrees with the sparse-index cksum -> 502 and
# evicted, fail_open -> served pending (no-store) and blocked once the async
# verdict lands; /api/v1/formats reports cargo as enforced.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.10.0. Green: ak-backend:1.11.0 and newer.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-scan-formats"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
